requirements.detail:
Rods and bars are manufactured from high-purity Phosphorous Deoxidized non-arsenical Copper (equivalent to Grade Cu-DHP or BS 2874 C106), demonstrating a minimum copper content of 99.90 percent (Cu + Ag >= 99.90% min). Highly restricted element limits are enforced to prevent cracking during hot fabrication:
a) Phosphorus (P): 0.013 to 0.050 percent (commonly 0.015 to 0.050%);
b) Arsenic (As): 0.05 percent Max (or 0.06% Max);
c) Lead (Pb): 0.01 percent Max (or 0.03% Max);
d) Iron (Fe): 0.03 percent Max (or 0.05% Max);
e) Other total impurities: 0.06 percent Max.

Rods are tested in both the 'As manufactured' (M) and 'Annealed' (O) conditions. Mechanical properties must satisfy specified ranges depending on the specific diameter/width across flats:
a) Tensile Strength typically ranges between 130 to 270 MPa (or 13 to 27.5 kg/mm²);
b) Elongation at break must be at least 40 percent in the Annealed (O) state.
